WEBVTT

00:02.354 --> 00:05.255
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:05.490 --> 00:09.052
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:09.162 --> 00:12.427
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:12.532 --> 00:15.330
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:15.768 --> 00:18.897
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:19.006 --> 00:21.998
<i>Lucky there's a man who
positively can do</i>

00:22.242 --> 00:23.903
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:24.011 --> 00:25.603
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:25.746 --> 00:30.480
<i>He's a family guy</i>

00:40.329 --> 00:41.296
Hey, Quagmire.

00:41.397 --> 00:44.127
<i>Peter, I want you and the guys
to come over to my house right now.</i>

00:44.233 --> 00:45.325
We're drinking. What for?

00:45.434 --> 00:47.095
<i>Just come over.
I want you to see something.</i>

00:47.203 --> 00:50.037
All right. Come on, guys.
We're going to Quagmire's.

00:50.140 --> 00:53.541
All right, hang on.
I gotta go to the bathroom first.

00:54.144 --> 00:55.441
Okay, let's go.

00:57.614 --> 01:00.778
Oh, finally! Come on. Come on.
Come on inside.

01:00.885 --> 01:03.217
Well, what is it? What's the big damn deal?

01:03.321 --> 01:04.379
Look.

01:05.923 --> 01:06.890
It's a cat.

01:06.991 --> 01:09.460
Yeah! I just got him today.
His name's James.

01:09.561 --> 01:11.529
Isn't he just the cutest thing
you've ever seen?

01:11.630 --> 01:12.619
Hi, James.

01:13.832 --> 01:15.424
Oh, my God!

01:15.534 --> 01:19.471
Watch when I scratch his bottom.
He sticks his fanny in the air.

01:19.606 --> 01:22.473
We have liftoff. We have liftoff.

01:24.077 --> 01:25.544
Come here, James.

01:26.546 --> 01:28.036
What the hell are we doing?

01:28.149 --> 01:29.980
Quagmire, since when do you like cats?

01:30.084 --> 01:32.746
Since I found this little guy
living under my house.

01:32.853 --> 01:34.184
I'll tell you this.

01:34.288 --> 01:37.416
I understand now why the pharaohs
worshipped these animals.

01:38.593 --> 01:41.255
Oh, look, Joe. He's making friends.

01:41.363 --> 01:42.523
Oh, sorry.

01:42.631 --> 01:44.462
You know what? It's all right, Quagmire.

01:44.566 --> 01:46.431
That leg is mostly pus.

01:53.176 --> 01:54.200
Okay. Here it comes, James.

01:54.310 --> 01:55.868
Here comes the part I was
telling you about.

01:58.314 --> 01:59.907
You're one of those!

02:04.087 --> 02:06.112
- I hate Quagmire lately.
- Me, too.

02:06.223 --> 02:08.590
That cat has totally
changed his personality.

02:08.693 --> 02:11.423
Yeah. Like, when I went over
to his house the other day.

02:13.331 --> 02:14.298
Who is it?

02:14.399 --> 02:17.459
It's me, Quagmire.
I need to borrow your lawnmower.

02:17.569 --> 02:18.798
Quagmire's not here.

02:18.904 --> 02:21.395
It's just me, James.
I'm supposed to watch the house.

02:21.507 --> 02:22.496
Come on, Quagmire.

02:22.608 --> 02:25.771
It's 97 degrees out here.
We're two grown men.

02:25.878 --> 02:28.312
Are you selling yarn? 'Cause I love yarn.

02:28.414 --> 02:30.645
No. I need to borrow your lawnmower.

02:30.784 --> 02:33.184
Oh, I don't think Quagmire
wants me to do that.

02:33.286 --> 02:34.275
Oh, come on.

02:34.387 --> 02:38.153
I don't think Quagmire appreciated
the condition you returned it in last time.

02:38.258 --> 02:40.193
- Glenn, can I just...
- No! You can't have it!

02:40.862 --> 02:42.523
Hey, guys. It's James' birthday tomorrow.

02:42.630 --> 02:44.222
Would you all sign his card?

02:44.332 --> 02:46.300
You want us to sign a card for your cat?

02:46.400 --> 02:48.698
Yeah. And don't just put your name.
Write something clever.

02:48.804 --> 02:50.795
God, I hate having to come up
with something on the spot.

02:50.906 --> 02:51.873
Um...

02:52.407 --> 02:56.605
"Have a mice day. Best fishes. Peter. "

02:57.045 --> 02:59.037
Thanks. That's great.

02:59.148 --> 03:00.137
Well, I gotta get going.

03:00.250 --> 03:02.718
I'm heading off to Vermont
to get James' birthday present.

03:02.819 --> 03:04.878
There's this neat little store
called Cattitudes

03:04.988 --> 03:08.424
that makes all this neat cat stuff.
See you guys later.

03:08.959 --> 03:09.926
What a queer.

03:10.027 --> 03:13.428
He's going all the way to Vermont
for cat gifts and whatnot?

03:13.530 --> 03:17.159
You can get a scratching post
down at Walmart for $2,

03:17.268 --> 03:19.737
pair of Lee jeans for $9.

03:19.938 --> 03:21.530
You know, they got seats for children now.

03:21.640 --> 03:25.098
You put them right in your car.
Supposed to make them safer.

03:25.210 --> 03:28.907
Only problem is you can't lean your seat
all the way back. Oh.

03:32.451 --> 03:37.013
We gotta do something about this.
His whole life is about that stupid cat.

03:37.123 --> 03:39.388
Hey, you know, the cat's alone
at Quagmire's right now.

03:39.493 --> 03:42.690
You know what we should do?
We should go over there and shave it.

03:42.796 --> 03:46.254
That's a great idea! Let's do it!
Let's shave the cat!

03:46.400 --> 03:48.027
Oh, boy! I usually only get this excited

03:48.135 --> 03:50.570
when they say the title of a movie
in the movie.

03:50.672 --> 03:52.765
<i>I'm telling you
these drug dealers represent</i>

03:52.874 --> 03:55.604
<i>a clear and present danger
to the United States!</i>

03:55.710 --> 03:58.144
He said it! He said it!

03:58.246 --> 04:01.580
<i>All I'm saying is what if this
is as good as it gets?</i>

04:01.684 --> 04:04.050
There it is! There it is!

04:04.153 --> 04:06.178
<i>The only way
for me to solve this crisis</i>

04:06.288 --> 04:09.052
<i>The Quest for Peace.</i>

04:09.191 --> 04:10.955
Oh, that's why they call it that.

04:19.169 --> 04:21.297
All right. The cat's gotta be in here.

04:21.405 --> 04:23.965
Hey, let's take a man-sized poop
in his cat box,

04:24.075 --> 04:26.009
so he thinks there's something
really wrong with him.

04:26.110 --> 04:27.475
There it is!

04:28.813 --> 04:29.974
Rock 'n' roll!

04:30.082 --> 04:33.210
Yeah, shaving time.
All right, hand me the razor.

04:37.289 --> 04:38.381
Oh, my God!

04:38.490 --> 04:39.582
Peter, you killed it!

04:39.692 --> 04:42.718
Will you guys relax?
He's got eight more lives.

04:42.829 --> 04:44.694
Okay, seven more lives.

04:44.797 --> 04:48.665
Six. Five. Four. Three.

04:48.768 --> 04:50.168
Peter, stop doing what you're doing.

04:50.270 --> 04:51.259
What do we do?

04:51.372 --> 04:52.532
All right. All right. I have an idea.

04:52.639 --> 04:55.608
How about we hide the cat's body
and leave that window open?

04:55.709 --> 04:57.574
And that way it'll seem like
the cat ran away.

04:57.678 --> 04:59.202
We'll never get away with that!

04:59.346 --> 05:03.750
Oh, we just might.
You see, I've got a lucky cat's foot.

05:07.222 --> 05:09.622
You know, Peter,
it's sort of adding insult to injury

05:09.724 --> 05:12.956
raiding Quagmire's fridge for beer
after you killed his cat.

05:13.062 --> 05:16.725
"Or is it?" is my response.

05:19.001 --> 05:20.367
Oh, crap!

05:20.470 --> 05:21.732
God, I hate cops.

05:21.838 --> 05:24.739
Almost as much as I hated
my overly sensitive car alarm.

05:41.293 --> 05:42.783
Son of a bitch!

05:43.362 --> 05:44.488
What do we got, partner?

05:44.596 --> 05:45.688
Empty alcohol containers.

05:45.798 --> 05:47.823
The driver's inebriated
and covered in blood.

05:47.933 --> 05:49.764
He's got scratches on his face and arms.

05:49.868 --> 05:51.632
There's a blood-soaked corpse
in the back seat.

05:51.738 --> 05:52.727
Got shovels in there,

05:52.839 --> 05:56.240
and a hand-drawn map titled
"This Is Where We'll Hide the Body. "

05:56.342 --> 05:59.573
Well, that all seems fine.
Sorry to bother you, sir.

06:02.316 --> 06:03.783
Pot! Small amount of pot!

06:03.884 --> 06:05.442
You're under arrest, dirtbag!

06:05.586 --> 06:06.575
Oh, come on!

06:06.687 --> 06:10.624
I don't appreciate drug addicts in my town!
I'm a family guy!

06:10.759 --> 06:12.920
He said it!

06:19.000 --> 06:22.027
All right, Brian.
Your family's here to bail you out.

06:22.138 --> 06:23.127
Brian, if you don't mind,

06:23.239 --> 06:25.332
we'll start thinking up
our prison-rape jokes immediately.

06:25.441 --> 06:26.499
I'll break the ice.

06:26.609 --> 06:29.874
Hey, Brian, did you do hard time?
Or hardly working?

06:31.515 --> 06:32.641
Penis.

06:33.317 --> 06:35.785
All right. All the pieces are there.
Somebody make something out of that.

06:35.886 --> 06:39.720
Hey, Brian. Who's your favorite
baseball player? Albert Pujols?

06:39.823 --> 06:44.056
Chris, stop it! Come on.
Brian, we're happy you're out of jail.

06:44.195 --> 06:47.289
And when we get to the car,
would you like a donut to sit on?

06:47.398 --> 06:53.338
You see? I'm part of it!
I'm part of it like everyone else!

06:53.539 --> 06:56.508
I can't believe they threw me in jail
for a quarter ounce of pot.

06:56.609 --> 07:00.204
Well, Brian, it's your own fault.
I mean, pot is illegal for a reason.

07:00.312 --> 07:02.508
Lois, don't be a hypocrite.
You've smoked pot.

07:02.616 --> 07:05.847
Well, sure, Brian,
but I'm thinking about the children.

07:05.952 --> 07:08.011
Pot's illegal mainly to protect them.

07:08.121 --> 07:11.285
No, no. Pot is illegal
because William Randolph Hearst

07:11.392 --> 07:14.691
ran a smear campaign against marijuana
in the 1930s

07:14.795 --> 07:17.286
to protect his interests
in the timber industry,

07:17.398 --> 07:20.629
because hemp was poised to replace wood
as an inexpensive raw material

07:20.735 --> 07:22.636
for the manufacture of paper.

07:24.640 --> 07:26.733
There's your smear campaign
right there, Brian.

07:27.943 --> 07:29.843
Mom's right. Drugs are bad, Brian.

07:29.945 --> 07:31.777
I mean, haven't you seen
those commercials?

08:16.563 --> 08:17.894
Open up, Brian. It's Joe.

08:17.998 --> 08:19.761
Crap! Just a sec.

08:24.239 --> 08:28.039
Brian, under your probation, you're
required to submit to random drug tests.

08:28.142 --> 08:29.131
I need some urine.

08:29.244 --> 08:30.609
You mean right now?

08:30.712 --> 08:31.975
Yes, right now.

08:32.081 --> 08:34.106
Here's some magazines to get you going.

08:34.216 --> 08:35.740
Uh, how's that gonna...

08:35.851 --> 08:37.910
Oh, sorry. It's been awhile.

08:38.020 --> 08:40.750
Look, I don't really feel comfortable
doing this in front of you.

08:40.856 --> 08:42.119
Fine. I'll wait outside.

08:42.225 --> 08:43.624
Here's a bottle of lotion.

08:43.727 --> 08:46.025
- Uh, Joe...
- Right, sorry.

08:46.997 --> 08:50.262
- Stewie, I need your urine!
- Really?

08:50.367 --> 08:51.595
Yeah. Joe is doing a drug test,

08:51.701 --> 08:53.966
and if I give him some of mine,
he's gonna know I've been smoking pot.

08:54.071 --> 08:56.232
So I need some of your urine, so I can...

08:56.340 --> 08:58.570
Uh, you don't have to be naked for this.

08:58.676 --> 09:01.338
But I don't have to not be naked
for it, either.

09:01.445 --> 09:03.175
Aha!

09:05.417 --> 09:07.942
Come on, Stewie. Hurry up and pee.
Joe's waiting for me.

09:08.053 --> 09:11.250
Brian, you know I can't go
unless you stare at it.

09:11.657 --> 09:12.852
Brian, what the hell?

09:12.959 --> 09:14.586
Uh, hey, Lois.

09:14.694 --> 09:17.094
The jig's up, Brian! Run!

09:17.897 --> 09:20.559
Brian, is this how you're trying
to pass your drug test?

09:20.667 --> 09:24.331
By stealing a baby's urine?
My God, that is just sick!

09:24.438 --> 09:26.463
No. What's sick is making marijuana illegal

09:26.573 --> 09:29.337
when it's been proven that it does
less damage to you than alcohol.

09:29.443 --> 09:32.277
<i>No. What's sick is the plot
of the movie Baby Mama.</i>

09:32.414 --> 09:34.712
<i>What happens
when a 40-year-old woman</i>

09:34.816 --> 09:38.274
<i>asks her 41-year-old friend
to carry her baby?</i>

09:38.486 --> 09:41.284
Push, Angie, push!
Push harder... Oh, it's dead.

09:41.389 --> 09:43.119
Brian, when you have to go
to these lengths

09:43.225 --> 09:46.558
just to get away with smoking pot,
it's time to make a change.

09:46.662 --> 09:48.789
You're right, Lois.
It is time to make a change.

09:48.898 --> 09:52.733
- Thank you.
- It's time for Quahog to legalize marijuana.

09:52.836 --> 09:54.895
What? That's not exactly what I meant.

09:55.005 --> 09:56.597
Hey, check out the size
of Stewie's penis.

09:56.707 --> 09:59.904
Oh, come on, guys!
It's just the way God made me.

10:03.348 --> 10:06.784
<i>No more oppression!
We as American adults with free will</i>

10:06.884 --> 10:09.546
<i>have the right to use marijuana
if we choose to!</i>

10:09.654 --> 10:12.715
<i>Enough government profiteering
under the guise of morality!</i>

10:12.825 --> 10:14.656
<i>Enough with this phony war on drugs!</i>

10:20.121 --> 10:22.146
You know, you're going about this
all wrong, Brian.

10:22.256 --> 10:25.420
If you want to win people over,
you can't just drone on like Ben Stein.

10:25.527 --> 10:27.188
You've got to have
a little more showmanship.

10:27.295 --> 10:28.694
Here, watch.

10:39.342 --> 10:42.779
<i>Now, everybody gather round
and listen if you would</i>

10:42.880 --> 10:46.281
<i>When I tell you every person needs
a way of feeling good</i>

10:46.383 --> 10:49.819
<i>Every kitty needs a ball of string
and every dog a stick</i>

10:49.920 --> 10:53.322
<i>But all you need is a bag of weed
to really get a kick</i>

10:53.758 --> 10:57.091
<i>One, two, three, four, five, six,
seven, eight!</i>

10:57.195 --> 10:58.719
<i>A bag o' weed, a bag o' weed</i>

10:58.830 --> 11:00.457
<i>Oh, everything is better
with a bag o' weed</i>

11:00.565 --> 11:02.157
<i>It's the only help that you'll ever need</i>

11:02.267 --> 11:04.361
<i>Because everything is better
with a bag o' weed!</i>

11:04.470 --> 11:07.166
There you go. You're all getting it now.

11:09.341 --> 11:10.968
<i>They go assault a queer</i>

11:12.778 --> 11:14.474
<i>They rent The Rocketeer</i>

11:16.283 --> 11:18.114
<i>- He humps a guy like me
- Right!</i>

11:18.218 --> 11:21.619
<i>But all we need is a bag o' weed
to keep us worry free</i>

11:21.988 --> 11:25.186
<i>One, two, three, ho!
A bag o' weed, a bag o' weed</i>

11:25.293 --> 11:26.920
<i>Oh, everything is better
with a bag o' weed</i>

11:27.028 --> 11:28.620
<i>No, you don't need meth
and you don't need speed</i>

11:28.730 --> 11:30.994
<i>Because everything is better
with a bag o' weed</i>

11:31.833 --> 11:33.426
Have a go, Brian.

11:34.103 --> 11:37.368
<i>As Mr. H. L. Mencken said
'"The common man's a fool'"</i>

11:37.573 --> 11:39.268
<i>And just like Helen Keller said...</i>

11:41.043 --> 11:43.740
<i>But try and use your heads
and don't buy into all the fear</i>

11:43.847 --> 11:44.814
Hey!

11:44.914 --> 11:48.077
<i>Because all we need is a bag o' weed
to make us want to cheer</i>

11:48.184 --> 11:50.812
<i>And one, two
A bag o' weed, a bag o' weed</i>

11:50.920 --> 11:52.512
<i>Oh, everything is better
with a bag o' weed</i>

11:52.622 --> 11:54.250
<i>You can try and fight but we're all agreed</i>

11:54.358 --> 11:57.384
<i>Because everything
is better with a bag o' weed</i>

13:04.268 --> 13:07.601
<i>One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight</i>

13:07.705 --> 13:09.366
<i>And a one, two, three, four</i>

13:09.473 --> 13:11.270
<i>And a five, and a six
and a seven. Oh!</i>

13:11.375 --> 13:12.899
<i>A bag o' weed, a bag o' weed</i>

13:13.010 --> 13:14.501
<i>Oh, everything is better
with a bag o' weed</i>

13:14.613 --> 13:16.376
<i>You're a happy guy
when you plant the seed</i>

13:16.481 --> 13:20.212
<i>Because everything is better
with a bag o' weed</i>

13:21.887 --> 13:24.755
<i>Oh, everything is better
with a bag o' weed!</i>

13:29.996 --> 13:33.955
As Mayor of Quahog, I hereby sign
into law the legalization of marijuana.

13:38.028 --> 13:41.964
Good evening, everyone.
Our top story, marijuana is now legal.

13:42.499 --> 13:44.661
Is now legal.

13:45.436 --> 13:47.529
Legal in Quahog.

13:48.106 --> 13:51.564
And it's made everything just so great.

13:51.776 --> 13:53.368
Okay, you... You can read the next one.

13:54.747 --> 13:56.112
- No, you can.
- No, you.

13:56.215 --> 13:57.443
Okay, okay, okay.

13:57.549 --> 13:59.039
- Let's read it both together.
- Okay.

13:59.151 --> 14:00.311
- Ready?
- Okay.

14:00.419 --> 14:03.877
Here's Ollie Williams
with a BlaccuWeather forecast.

14:04.356 --> 14:05.722
How's the weather look, Ollie?

14:05.825 --> 14:07.156
Not too bad.

14:07.260 --> 14:08.488
Right on.

14:08.762 --> 14:11.560
See, Lois? Tell me things in Quahog
aren't better now.

14:11.665 --> 14:12.927
It's just weird, Brian.

14:13.033 --> 14:15.594
I still don't think I'm comfortable
with the whole idea.

14:15.703 --> 14:18.968
Look, Lois, ever since marijuana
was legalized, crime has gone down,

14:19.073 --> 14:22.406
<i>productivity is up, and ratings
for Doctor Who are through the roof.</i>

14:22.510 --> 14:26.379
Yeah. But Peter's so baked lately
he can hardly set up a cutaway.

14:26.481 --> 14:30.918
Man! This is even better than... No, wait.

14:31.019 --> 14:35.457
No, this is worse than... Better...
I don't know.

14:35.558 --> 14:37.549
Here's a list of celebrities I don't like.

15:12.965 --> 15:14.193
Hello, Griffin.

15:14.300 --> 15:16.132
Mr. Pewterschmidt? Hey, how you been?

15:16.236 --> 15:17.203
Not good.

15:17.337 --> 15:20.363
I'm sorry to hear that. Wow! A limo, huh?

15:20.474 --> 15:22.374
Hey, are these Diet Rites just to take?

15:22.476 --> 15:24.740
No! Those are my Diet Rites!

15:24.845 --> 15:25.835
Now, listen, Griffin.

15:25.947 --> 15:28.381
Thanks to your dog's
stupid marijuana crusade,

15:28.483 --> 15:32.817
Fabric, fuel and paper.

15:33.187 --> 15:35.952
Which means I'm losing billions
in timber dollars.

15:36.058 --> 15:37.889
I had to sell my Bangles records.

15:37.993 --> 15:40.257
I was still working
on memorizing all the words.

15:40.596 --> 15:43.724
<i>My back is hurting
from the chair I'm sitting on</i>

15:43.832 --> 15:45.163
<i>Where's the Tylenol?</i>

15:45.267 --> 15:49.568
<i>If I lay down flat on the floor
it usually kind of fixes it</i>

15:49.906 --> 15:56.779
<i>Tony Danza from Who's the Boss?
Says, '"A-oh, a-oh, oh-a, oh-a-oh! '"</i>

15:57.548 --> 16:00.039
I'm losing money, and it's your dog's fault.

16:00.151 --> 16:01.914
Now, I have to get hemp illegalized again,

16:02.019 --> 16:04.817
and the only way to do that
is to start a fear campaign

16:04.922 --> 16:07.391
designed to turn people against pot.

16:07.492 --> 16:08.459
Will you help me?

16:08.560 --> 16:11.688
Gosh, Mr. Pewterschmidt,
I could never go against Brian like that.

16:11.797 --> 16:14.288
I'll give you this light-up butterfly yo-yo.

16:14.399 --> 16:16.391
- To keep?
- Not to keep!

16:16.502 --> 16:18.936
You can use it today
and one more day in the summer.

16:19.038 --> 16:20.665
- Yeah!
- Pull over.

16:29.383 --> 16:30.350
Bye.

16:33.120 --> 16:36.090
All right, Carter. I finished
cutting together our anti-pot video.

16:36.191 --> 16:37.556
Take a look.

16:37.792 --> 16:41.956
"Hey, I got a great idea.
Let's kill six million Jews. "

16:42.063 --> 16:46.023
"Hooray! Yeah! Yeah, I'm on
board! How did you come up with that?"

16:46.135 --> 16:50.469
"I got the idea from... From...
Well, from while I was smoking pot.

16:50.840 --> 16:53.866
"Anybody else who likes pot,
reach for my joint. "

16:54.143 --> 16:56.612
"Oh, there it is!
Give us some of that!"

16:57.814 --> 16:58.872
"Perhaps later.

16:58.982 --> 17:03.248
<i>"Now, let's go to France
and steal all their objects de art. '"</i>

17:03.353 --> 17:05.446
"All right!
Let's go to France. "

17:05.555 --> 17:06.716
Not bad, eh?

17:06.824 --> 17:09.088
Damn it! That was Fox News.

17:09.193 --> 17:11.058
Apparently, they own the rights
to Hitler's likeness

17:11.162 --> 17:12.789
and they won't have him slandered.

17:16.335 --> 17:17.359
Hi, I'm Peter.

17:17.469 --> 17:21.303
<i>You know me from the movie Harold,
Kumar & Peter Go to White Castle.</i>

17:21.406 --> 17:24.933
As you can see, I am enjoying
a White Castle burger. Why?

17:25.043 --> 17:26.739
Because I don't do drugs.

17:26.846 --> 17:29.280
Took me five minutes
to get to White Castle.

17:29.382 --> 17:32.374
I didn't get diverted
by all those crazy high jinks.

17:32.485 --> 17:34.453
'Cause I don't get high.

17:35.555 --> 17:37.615
It was a good movie, though.

17:37.958 --> 17:39.585
You know Neil Patrick Harris got the job

17:39.693 --> 17:42.423
<i>on How I Met Your Mother
'cause of that movie?</i>

17:42.530 --> 17:43.622
You know, I've only seen that show once,

17:43.731 --> 17:45.961
but I gotta tell you,
what's really weird to me is

17:46.066 --> 17:49.503
why is the voice of the guy
from the future Bob Saget?

17:49.604 --> 17:52.334
I mean, the guy on the show,
he's already an adult, you know?

17:52.440 --> 17:55.375
So it's not like he's gonna
grow into Bob Saget.

17:55.477 --> 17:57.309
It doesn't make sense.

17:57.647 --> 17:59.444
Thank you for your time.

17:59.549 --> 18:00.607
Well, what do you think?

18:00.716 --> 18:03.082
Look, Daddy,
I agree with what you're trying to do,

18:03.186 --> 18:06.918
but I just don't think this is gonna work.
It's so artificial.

18:07.024 --> 18:08.821
You're asking for a spanking, young lady.

18:08.926 --> 18:10.257
- Yeah!
All right!

18:10.360 --> 18:12.521
Peter, the reason Brian succeeded
in his cause

18:12.629 --> 18:15.120
is that he spoke with such passion.

18:15.232 --> 18:18.066
No offense, but you two just
don't have that talent.

18:18.169 --> 18:20.899
Are you kidding? I can be very persuasive.

18:21.005 --> 18:25.533
That's how I used to lure wayward sailors
to their deaths with my siren song.

18:54.909 --> 18:58.311
Hello, Brian. You're looking good.
Nice shiny coat.

18:58.413 --> 19:00.677
Don't try to butter me up, Carter.
Why did you call me here?

19:00.782 --> 19:03.307
Come inside.
There's something I want to show you.

19:08.057 --> 19:09.024
What's this?

19:09.125 --> 19:12.583
<i>It's your novel, Brian,
Faster than the Speed of Love.</i>

19:13.029 --> 19:14.690
Ready to ship out tomorrow.

19:14.797 --> 19:17.733
All you have to do is publicly
come out against pot.

19:17.835 --> 19:20.201
Forget it, Carter.
I'm not gonna take your bribe.

19:20.304 --> 19:22.067
I don't care if you printed a million copies.

19:22.172 --> 19:23.730
I printed two million.

19:23.841 --> 19:27.778
And I even commissioned an oil painting
for your author's photo.

19:28.546 --> 19:29.740
And what's this?

19:29.848 --> 19:33.284
Is this an Oprah Book Club sticker?
I think it is.

19:33.385 --> 19:35.615
Wait. Really? Oh, my God!

19:35.720 --> 19:38.451
Plus, I can get you a night in bed
with Oprah.

19:39.659 --> 19:42.287
Okay, just the sticker then.
So what do you say? Is it a deal?

19:42.395 --> 19:44.329
You don't have to sell out like this, Brian!

19:45.631 --> 19:50.729
Your novel is good enough
to be published on its own merits.

19:50.837 --> 19:53.135
- You think so?
- Yeah, you bet.

19:53.473 --> 19:56.931
This is your shot, Brian.
You can be a superstar author.

19:57.411 --> 20:01.143
All you got to do is make an impassioned
anti-pot speech in public.

20:01.249 --> 20:02.238
Forget it, Carter!

20:02.350 --> 20:04.318
Even Stewie says the book
is good enough on its own.

20:04.419 --> 20:05.477
Right, Stewie?

20:07.088 --> 20:09.580
Maybe do a song about why pot is bad.

20:09.692 --> 20:12.388
<i>And that's why pot is bad</i>

20:14.730 --> 20:17.757
<i>I've heard all I need to make
an informed decision.</i>

20:17.867 --> 20:21.268
<i>Marijuana is hereby re-illegalized.</i>

20:26.176 --> 20:29.044
<i>In other news,
a local Quahog author has set a record</i>

20:29.146 --> 20:31.671
<i>for the worst-selling novel of all time.</i>

20:31.782 --> 20:34.182
<i>Brian Griffin's
Faster than the Speed of Love</i>

20:34.285 --> 20:36.719
<i>has astonishingly not sold a single copy</i>

20:36.821 --> 20:39.916
<i>thanks to universal panning
by literary critics.</i>

20:40.025 --> 20:43.392
<i>Coming up, children are getting sexier,
and that's...</i>

20:43.929 --> 20:45.624
<i>That's pretty cool.</i>

20:46.031 --> 20:49.229
This is so humiliating.
I sold out everything I believed in,

20:49.335 --> 20:52.566
and I have nothing to show for it.
My book's a bomb.

20:52.672 --> 20:55.539
Well, look at it this way.
You did accomplish something.

20:55.641 --> 20:57.632
Marijuana's illegal because of you,

20:57.744 --> 21:01.738
and Stewie got to build a nice little fort
with all of your unsold books.

21:01.849 --> 21:03.908
My house is made of mediocrity.

21:06.587 --> 21:09.489
Hey, guys. I want you to know
I'm raising my reward to $50

21:09.591 --> 21:12.958
for anyone who can help me find James.
No questions asked.

21:13.061 --> 21:14.653
I killed your cat.

21:14.654 --> 22:15.654
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru